A||N||8||jaguiler||Question - easy one for you guys!||||1||
Z||000000||jaguiler||04-04-2001||08:44 PM||||Ok.... I have been looking on how to chk the fluid level on manual transmission.  I know you are supposed to pull out the speedo cable,  but I don't know which one that is.  I have not had too much time to look at it in the daylight....but how do I identify it's location?  I saw two plugs in the tranny.  One near the back and another near the drivers side wheel, covered by some shifter cables, (i think)  Is the tranny fluid shared with the clutch?  are they the same case?  or are they two sep. things I have to take care of....  <BR>I know my question is basic, but I have not had too much time with the car...  <P>In other words how do I find my speedo cable and sensor?<P>thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000001||danny boy||04-04-2001||08:58 PM|||| Find the shift linkage. look between it and the trunk. There will be a round thing(VSS) with an electrical connector in it. remove the plug, take out the 10 mm bolt, pull the whole thing out carefully so you dont pull the gear off and lose it in the tranny, and there you go.||||reg||1
Z||000002||85Josh||04-04-2001||09:01 PM||||The clutch itself is dry, the hydraulic system is the actuating system and is seperate from the tranny. The clutch master cylinder and fluid reservoir are under the hood, just below the brake master cylinder.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000003||jaguiler||04-04-2001||11:02 PM||||So the clutch is dry?.... ok so the tranny has the oil in it....makes sense.... one more thing...how do I find the shift linkage?  I found two plugs in that general area....one near the trunk....... and another near the drivers side wheel....  which is it?  They both have electrical connections that go to them.  I know my question is basic but I am planning to chk the level this weekend and need to know.<BR>The Hanyes manual had a pic.  but I had trouble finding it in the car too.....<P><BR>Thanks<P><BR> <P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||04-04-2001||11:18 PM||||The one nearest the trunk is the VSS (vehicle speed sensor). You have no 'cable', The one near the drivers side wheel well is the back-up light switch.<BR>Is your car a 4 cylinder or a V-6? The V-6 (5 speed) should have a 'dip stick'. As noted above, if you remove the VSS, take care NOT TO LOOSE THE GEAR inside the transmission! If it is low on fluid, use motor oil (5W-30) to top off.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||04-04-2001||11:24 PM||||The v6 5 speed (Getrag) has a dipstick.<BR>The VSS is on the right side of the differential, the dipstick is on the left side of the differential.<P>The 4 speeds are the only transmissions that require the VSS to be removed to check fluid level.||||reg||1
Z||000006||85Josh||04-04-2001||11:31 PM||||Uh, Will, the Isuzu 5-speeds under 4-cyls also uses the VSS as a dipstick. I lost my !@@#$#$%^ speedo gear the last time I check my tranny oil, and the POS jammed my shift linkage.||||reg||1
Z||000007||jaguiler||04-04-2001||11:36 PM||||OK I have an 86 GT - V^ - 5 speed.... I think I got my answer...it is the plug closest to the trunk on the drivers side.... with 2 wires coming from it.... if I'm wrong please correct me...<BR>Thanks everyone!<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||04-04-2001||11:38 PM||||Mine has a little dipstick that says "TRANS FLUID", I thought all Getrags had this.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">  <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I>||||reg||12
